**First pending task** (TASK-008/009/010/016/017/018/019 blocked; TASK-020–025 completed). The Experience build TASK-025's note pointed to next.

**Acceptance criterion** — *"Events have unique IDs and timestamps; duplicate taps do not double-count; offline entries sync without loss"* — met exactly:

| Requirement | How |
|---|---|
| Unique IDs + timestamps | Every completion → `CompletionEvent` with `crypto.randomUUID` (+ fallback) id and a `completedAt` ms timestamp stamped at the tap |
| No double-count | Recording is **idempotent on a client key** — one gesture = one key; any replay returns the stored event (`added:false`), never a second row |
| Offline sync without loss | Offline-first durable writes + a `pending→synced` lifecycle: a failed/offline flush keeps every event pending and retries; partial confirms re-queue the rest; re-flush is idempotent |

